  "name": "itree-program-logic",
  "description": "A Coq-based framework for constructing modular program logics by integrating Interaction Trees with the Iris separation logic framework. It facilitates the definition of compositional operational semantics and the derivation of adequate program logics for diverse language features, including angelic non-determinism, shared memory, and concurrent thread pools.",
